Write the entire honest compact raw JSON exclusively, then execute the prompt's exact literal pinned adapter command through `functions.exec`/`tools.exec_command` inside the same fresh CLI session before completion. This additional authorized command writes only the two deterministic compatibility files. Do not hand-write exports, hide the call in a wrapper or variable, edit the compact raw afterward, or run an export after the CLI ends. The runner pins all three actual files in its immutable completion; the packet and launch inputs pin adapter, method, addendum, binding audit, preparer, existing rubric/rules/helpers, and all exact source/poster assets. Adapter errors preserve raw/error evidence and make the recording procedural NA; they do not authorize rewriting raw, a replacement review, another session, or extra image generation.

`audit_compact_bindings.py` joins those immutable pins and reproduces exports read-only. It checks a recognized successful exact adapter invocation before turn completion; unfamiliar trace serialization is NA, not a claimed tool event. Semantic image viewing and the quality of judgments remain critic attestations. Existing v4 summary thresholds continue to operate on the compatibility exports; the binding audit and existing source-attestation audit must also remain valid. No average, cherry-picking, extra reviews, or gate relaxation is introduced.

